M=[
("loto","med","Before working on a PTAC unit's wiring, what must you do?","Antes de trabajar en el cableado de un PTAC, ¿qué debes hacer?",["Shut off and lock out the power, then verify it's dead","Just turn it off at the remote","Work fast","Unplug it halfway"],["Cortar y bloquear la energía, y comprobar que no haya corriente","Solo apagarlo con el control","Trabajar rápido","Desconectarlo a medias"],"Lockout/tagout prevents someone from turning power back on while you work.","El bloqueo y etiquetado evita que alguien vuelva a dar energía mientras trabajas.",LOTO),
("loto","hard","After locking out a breaker, what's the next step before touching wires?","Después de bloquear un breaker, ¿qué sigue antes de tocar los cables?",["Test with a meter to confirm there's no voltage","Touch the wire quickly to check","Assume it's off","Remove the lock"],["Probar con un multímetro que no haya voltaje","Tocar el cable rápido para ver","Suponer que ya está apagado","Quitar el candado"],"Verify zero energy — breakers can be mislabeled.","Comprueba que no haya energía; los breakers pueden estar mal rotulados.",LOTO),
("loto","med","Who removes a lockout lock?","¿Quién quita un candado de bloqueo?",["Only the person who put it on","Whoever needs the equipment","The front desk","Any manager without checking"],["Solo la persona que lo puso","Quien necesite el equipo","La recepción","Cualquier gerente sin revisar"],"Your lock, your key — that's what keeps you safe.","Tu candado, tu llave; así te mantienes seguro.",LOTO),
("ladder","easy","How many points of contact should you keep when climbing a ladder?","¿Cuántos puntos de apoyo debes mantener al subir una escalera?",["Three — two hands and a foot, or two feet and a hand","One","Two feet only","Zero if it's short"],["Tres: dos manos y un pie, o dos pies y una mano","Uno","Solo los dos pies","Ninguno si es corta"],"Three points of contact is OSHA's basic ladder rule.","Tres puntos de apoyo es la regla básica de OSHA para escaleras.",LAD),
("ladder","med","An extension ladder should extend how far above the roof edge you step onto?","¿Cuánto debe sobresalir una escalera de extensión del borde del techo al que te subes?",["At least 3 feet","6 inches","It shouldn't extend past it","10 feet"],["Al menos 3 pies","6 pulgadas","No debe sobresalir","10 pies"],"OSHA requires side rails to extend at least 3 feet above the landing.","OSHA exige que los rieles sobresalgan al menos 3 pies del punto de apoyo.",LAD),
("ladder","easy","A stepladder's top cap says 'Do not stand.' Why?","La tapa de una escalera de tijera dice 'No pararse aquí'. ¿Por qué?",["You can lose balance and tip it over","It's only a sticker","It's for paint cans only","It's fine for quick jobs"],["Puedes perder el equilibrio y voltearla","Es solo una calcomanía","Es solo para botes de pintura","Está bien para trabajos rápidos"],"Use a taller ladder instead of the top cap.","Usa una escalera más alta en lugar de pararte en la tapa.",LAD),
("electrical","med","A GFCI outlet in a bathroom won't reset. What does that tell you?","Un contacto GFCI del baño no se restablece. ¿Qué te indica?",["There may be a ground fault or bad outlet — investigate before using it","Nothing, use another plug","Tape the button down","It needs a bigger fuse"],["Puede haber falla a tierra o el contacto está dañado; revisa antes de usarlo","Nada, usa otro contacto","Pegarle cinta al botón","Necesita un fusible más grande"],"GFCIs trip to prevent shock near water.","Los GFCI se botan para evitar descargas cerca del agua.",ELEC),
("electrical","easy","Why are GFCI outlets required near sinks and tubs?","¿Por qué se requieren contactos GFCI cerca de lavabos y tinas?",["They cut power fast to prevent shock near water","They charge phones faster","They save electricity","They look nicer"],["Cortan la corriente rápido para evitar descargas cerca del agua","Cargan más rápido los celulares","Ahorran electricidad","Se ven mejor"],"Water and electricity are a deadly mix; GFCIs react in milliseconds.","El agua y la electricidad son peligrosas; los GFCI reaccionan en milisegundos.",ELEC),
("legionella","hard","Why flush water in guest rooms that haven't been used for a while?","¿Por qué dejar correr el agua en cuartos que no se han usado en un tiempo?",["Stagnant water can grow Legionella bacteria","To test water pressure only","To clean the tub","It's not needed"],["El agua estancada puede generar la bacteria Legionella","Solo para probar la presión","Para limpiar la tina","No hace falta"],"Legionella grows in still, lukewarm water and spreads through showerhead mist.","La Legionella crece en agua quieta y tibia y se transmite por el vapor de la regadera.",LEG),
("legionella","hard","What hot-water practice helps control Legionella?","¿Qué práctica de agua caliente ayuda a controlar la Legionella?",["Keep the water heater hot enough per the water management plan and avoid stagnant lines","Set it as low as possible","Turn it off at night","Only use cold water"],["Mantener el calentador lo bastante caliente según el plan de manejo de agua y evitar líneas estancadas","Ponerlo lo más bajo posible","Apagarlo de noche","Usar solo agua fría"],"Lukewarm water is the danger zone. Follow the hotel's water management plan.","El agua tibia es la zona de riesgo. Sigue el plan de manejo de agua del hotel.",LEG),
("co","med","A guest reports a headache and the CO alarm chirps near the boiler room. What do you do?","Un huésped reporta dolor de cabeza y la alarma de CO suena cerca del cuarto de calderas. ¿Qué haces?",["Get people out to fresh air, call 911, and don't re-enter","Silence the alarm and keep working","Open a window and stay","Wait for it to stop"],["Sacar a la gente al aire libre, llamar al 911 y no volver a entrar","Silenciar la alarma y seguir","Abrir una ventana y quedarte","Esperar a que pare"],"Carbon monoxide is invisible and odorless. Evacuate and call for help.","El monóxido de carbono no se ve ni se huele. Evacua y pide ayuda.",CO),
("co","easy","Which equipment can produce carbon monoxide in a hotel?","¿Qué equipo puede producir monóxido de carbono en un hotel?",["Gas boilers, water heaters and dryers","LED lights","TVs","Ice machines"],["Calderas, calentadores y secadoras de gas","Focos LED","Televisiones","Máquinas de hielo"],"Anything that burns fuel can make CO if it's not venting right.","Todo lo que quema combustible puede generar CO si no ventila bien.",CO),
("fire","easy","What does PASS stand for when using a fire extinguisher?","¿Qué significa PASS al usar un extintor?",["Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep","Push, Alarm, Spray, Stop","Point, Ask, Shoot, Stand","Pull, Alert, Spray, Shut"],["Jalar, Apuntar, Apretar, Barrer","Empujar, Alarma, Rociar, Parar","Señalar, Preguntar, Disparar, Pararse","Jalar, Alertar, Rociar, Cerrar"],"Aim at the base of the fire and sweep side to side.","Apunta a la base del fuego y barre de lado a lado.",EXT),
("fire","med","How often should portable fire extinguishers get a quick visual check?","¿Cada cuánto se deben revisar a simple vista los extintores portátiles?",["Monthly","Every 5 years only","Never","Only after a fire"],["Cada mes","Solo cada 5 años","Nunca","Solo después de un incendio"],"OSHA requires monthly visual inspections and annual maintenance.","OSHA pide revisión visual mensual y mantenimiento anual.",EXT),
("fire","med","A sprinkler head in a room is painted over. What should happen?","Un rociador de un cuarto está pintado. ¿Qué debe pasar?",["Report it — it may need replacing by a licensed contractor","Scrape the paint off with a knife","Leave it","Hang a hanger on it"],["Reportarlo; puede necesitar reemplazo por un contratista certificado","Rasparle la pintura con un cuchillo","Dejarlo así","Colgarle un gancho"],"Paint can stop a sprinkler from opening in a fire.","La pintura puede impedir que el rociador funcione en un incendio.","https://www.nfpa.org/codes-and-standards/nfpa-25-standard-development/25"),
("pool","med","Who should adjust pool chemicals?","¿Quién debe ajustar los químicos de la alberca?",["Only trained staff following the hotel's pool procedure and MN rules","Anyone with a bucket","Guests","Housekeeping"],["Solo personal capacitado siguiendo el procedimiento del hotel y las reglas de MN","Cualquiera con una cubeta","Los huéspedes","Limpieza"],"Pool chemicals are dangerous and regulated by the MN Department of Health.","Los químicos de alberca son peligrosos y los regula el Departamento de Salud de MN.",POOL),
("pool","hard","Why must pool chemicals like chlorine and acid be stored apart?","¿Por qué se guardan por separado químicos de alberca como cloro y ácido?",["Mixing them can release toxic chlorine gas","They look alike","To save space","They expire faster together"],["Al mezclarse pueden soltar gas de cloro tóxico","Se parecen","Para ahorrar espacio","Caducan más rápido juntos"],"Store separately, labeled, and never add water to concentrated chemicals.","Guárdalos separados y etiquetados, y nunca les eches agua a los concentrados.",HAZ),
("winter","med","What's the main risk when the heat fails in a room during a Minnesota cold snap?","¿Cuál es el riesgo principal si falla la calefacción de un cuarto en una ola de frío en Minnesota?",["Frozen and burst pipes, plus an unsafe room for guests","Brighter lights","Louder TV","Nothing"],["Tuberías congeladas o reventadas, y un cuarto inseguro para el huésped","Luces más brillantes","Tele más fuerte","Nada"],"Prioritize heat calls in winter and move guests if needed.","En invierno, prioriza las fallas de calefacción y cambia al huésped de cuarto si hace falta.",COLD,("11-15","03-15")),
("winter","med","Before winter, what should you check on outdoor faucets?","Antes del invierno, ¿qué revisas en las llaves de agua exteriores?",["Shut off and drain them so they don't freeze","Leave hoses attached","Turn them on full","Paint them"],["Cerrarlas y drenarlas para que no se congelen","Dejar las mangueras conectadas","Abrirlas por completo","Pintarlas"],"Attached hoses trap water that freezes and cracks pipes.","Las mangueras conectadas atrapan agua que se congela y rompe tubos.",COLD,("09-15","11-30")),
("hvac","easy","Why change PTAC and HVAC filters on schedule?","¿Por qué cambiar a tiempo los filtros de los PTAC y del HVAC?",["Clean filters improve air, comfort and unit life","It's only for looks","It makes units louder","Filters never matter"],["Los filtros limpios mejoran el aire, la comodidad y la vida del equipo","Solo es por apariencia","Hace más ruido el equipo","No importan"],"Dirty filters cause weak airflow, odors and breakdowns.","Los filtros sucios causan poco aire, olores y fallas.",BP),
("hvac","med","A PTAC is dripping water inside the room. Most common cause?","Un PTAC gotea agua dentro del cuarto. ¿Cuál es la causa más común?",["A clogged condensate drain or unit not tilted to drain outside","The TV is too close","Too many towels","The light is on"],["Un drenaje de condensado tapado o el equipo no inclinado hacia afuera","La tele está muy cerca","Demasiadas toallas","La luz está prendida"],"Clear the drain and check the unit's pitch.","Destapa el drenaje y revisa la inclinación del equipo.",BP),
("plumbing","easy","A toilet keeps running after flushing. What's the likely fix?","Un inodoro sigue corriendo después de jalarle. ¿Qué es lo más probable?",["Adjust or replace the flapper or fill valve","Replace the whole toilet","Ignore it","Turn off the hotel's water"],["Ajustar o cambiar el sapo (flapper) o la válvula de llenado","Cambiar todo el inodoro","Ignorarlo","Cortar el agua del hotel"],"A running toilet wastes a lot of water and keeps guests up.","Un inodoro que corre desperdicia mucha agua y no deja dormir.",BP),
("plumbing","med","Water is leaking through a ceiling from the room above. What's first?","Se está filtrando agua del techo desde el cuarto de arriba. ¿Qué es lo primero?",["Find the source above and shut off that water, then protect the room below","Paint the ceiling","Wait until checkout","Put a bucket and leave"],["Buscar el origen arriba y cerrar esa agua, luego proteger el cuarto de abajo","Pintar el techo","Esperar a la salida","Poner una cubeta e irte"],"Stop the water first; then deal with damage and guests.","Primero corta el agua; después atiende los daños y a los huéspedes.",BP),
("work_orders","easy","Why log every repair in the work order system?","¿Por qué registrar cada reparación en el sistema de órdenes de trabajo?",["It tracks repeat problems, parts and rooms out of order","It's just paperwork","For the guest to see","It isn't needed"],["Lleva el control de fallas repetidas, piezas y cuartos fuera de servicio","Es solo papeleo","Para que lo vea el huésped","No hace falta"],"Good records show what to fix for good and what to budget.","Un buen registro muestra qué arreglar de fondo y qué presupuestar.",BP),
("work_orders","med","Which work order do you do first?","¿Qué orden de trabajo atiendes primero?",["Safety and guest-occupied problems, like no heat or a leak","Touch-up paint in a hallway","A squeaky door in storage","Changing a light in the office"],["Lo de seguridad y cuartos ocupados, como falta de calefacción o una fuga","Retocar pintura en un pasillo","Una puerta que rechina en la bodega","Cambiar un foco en la oficina"],"Safety first, then guests, then preventive work.","Primero seguridad, luego huéspedes, luego mantenimiento preventivo.",BP),
("elevator","med","A guest is stuck in the elevator. What do you do?","Un huésped está atrapado en el elevador. ¿Qué haces?",["Talk to them to keep calm and call the elevator company or 911 — don't force the doors","Pry open the doors","Shut off the building power","Tell them to climb out"],["Hablarle para calmarlo y llamar a la compañía de elevadores o al 911; no forzar las puertas","Abrir las puertas con palanca","Cortar la luz del edificio","Decirle que se salga trepando"],"Only elevator technicians or firefighters should do rescues.","Solo técnicos de elevadores o bomberos deben hacer rescates.",BP),
("ppe","easy","When using a grinder or drill, what protects your eyes?","Al usar una esmeriladora o taladro, ¿qué protege tus ojos?",["Safety glasses or goggles","Regular glasses only","Squinting","Nothing if it's quick"],["Lentes o gafas de seguridad","Solo tus lentes normales","Entrecerrar los ojos","Nada si es rápido"],"Flying debris causes many workplace eye injuries.","Las partículas que salen volando causan muchas lesiones de ojos en el trabajo.","https://www.osha.gov/eye-face-protection"),
("chemicals","med","You're using a strong drain cleaner. Where's the safest place to check its PPE needs?","Vas a usar un destapacaños fuerte. ¿Dónde revisas qué protección necesitas?",["The label and SDS","Online reviews","Ask a guest","Guess"],["La etiqueta y la SDS","Reseñas en internet","Preguntarle a un huésped","Adivinar"],"Drain cleaners can cause serious burns. The SDS lists the PPE.","Los destapacaños pueden causar quemaduras graves. La SDS dice qué protección usar.",HAZ),
("security","med","Why must a guest room lock be fixed the same day it's reported?","¿Por qué se debe arreglar el mismo día una chapa de cuarto que se reporta?",["An unsecured room is a safety risk and can't be sold","It only affects the look","Guests don't care","It can wait a week"],["Un cuarto sin seguridad es un riesgo y no se puede vender","Solo afecta la apariencia","A los huéspedes no les importa","Puede esperar una semana"],"Locks, deadbolts and door closers protect guests — top priority.","Las chapas, cerrojos y cierrapuertas protegen al huésped; son prioridad.",BP),
("fire","hard","Why must fire doors close and latch on their own?","¿Por qué las puertas contra incendio deben cerrar y trabarse solas?",["They slow smoke and fire from spreading","To keep the hall quiet","For privacy","They don't need to"],["Frenan el humo y el fuego para que no se extiendan","Para que el pasillo esté callado","Por privacidad","No hace falta"],"Report any fire door that doesn't close fully.","Reporta cualquier puerta contra incendio que no cierre bien.","https://www.nfpa.org/codes-and-standards/nfpa-80-standard-development/80"),
]
for t in M: n(MT,*t)
